{{!
    @template tool_vae/compare_diff

    The block of the comparison of two versions: the text kept as it is, what was added underlined, what was removed struck
    through, each with its words for a screen reader. The block keeps white space as written: on one logical line, each
    break carried by a comment, nothing between its tags and the runs.

    Every text comes from the context, given by tool_vae\output\compare_diff. The template holds no logic. Every value is
    escaped (double braces): none of them is HTML.

    Classes required for JS:
    * none

    Data attributes required for JS:
    * none

    Context variables required for this template:
    * added - string, the words that say a run was added
    * removed - string, the words that say a run was removed
    * runs - list of {equal, insert, remove, text}: each run, its kind (one of the three booleans) and its text

    Example context (json):
    {
        "added": "added:",
        "removed": "removed:",
        "runs": [
            {"equal": true, "insert": false, "remove": false, "text": "Je "},
            {"equal": false, "insert": false, "remove": true, "text": "prépare"},
            {"equal": false, "insert": true, "remove": false, "text": "range"}
        ]
    }
}}
<div class="tool-vae-diff border rounded p-3" style="white-space: pre-wrap;">{{#runs}}{{#equal}}{{text}}{{/equal}}{{!
}}{{#insert}}<ins class="tool-vae-ins"><span class="sr-only">{{added}} </span>{{text}}</ins>{{/insert}}{{!
}}{{#remove}}<del class="tool-vae-del"><span class="sr-only">{{removed}} </span>{{text}}</del>{{/remove}}{{/runs}}</div>
